course: dictionary
lesson: 8168
title: Resident: who lives here?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A resident is a person who lives in a place, such as a house, street, town or country. «Antarctica has no permanent residents, only scientists and staff who stay for a season or a year.» The word permanent means for always, so the sentence tells you that nobody lives there all the time.
explain: A resident can also be someone staying for a while in a hotel, care home or hospital. As an adjective, resident means living or working in a place: «our resident cat» is a cat that lives in your home all the time.
explain: Use context clues to check. A sign that says «residents only» on a street tells you that only people who live on that street may park there. Ask yourself: who lives here? That question is the clue.
explain: Some people use resident in a funny way. «The resident expert» is the person in a group who knows the most about something, like the family member who always knows how to fix the Wi-Fi.
fact: A resident is a person who lives in a place, such as a house, street, town or country.
fact: «Residents only» on a parking sign means only people who live there may park.
fact: A permanent resident lives in a place for good, not just for a short visit.
fact: As an adjective, «resident» means living or working in a place: «the resident artist» works in that place all the time.
fact: In science, an animal that lives in one area all year is a resident, not a visitor.
exercise: «Antarctica has no permanent residents, only scientists and staff who stay for a season or a year.» What is a resident? | A kind of weather | A visitor who stays only one day | A map of a town | *A person who lives in a place
exercise: A sign on a street says «residents only». Who may park there? | Visitors from other towns | Delivery vans only | Anyone with a bike | *People who live on that street
exercise: «Our resident cat sleeps on the sofa every day.» What does resident mean here? | Very fast | *Living in the house all the time | Hungry | Sleeping outside
test: Ava says, «He is the resident expert on dinosaurs.» What does resident mean here? | Angry | *Living or working in the group, and knowing the most | Tiny | Always lost
test: Which person is a resident of a hospital? | A doctor visiting for one hour | A window cleaner | A lost dog | *A patient staying there for a while
exam: «Antarctica has no permanent residents, only scientists and staff who stay for a season or a year.» What does permanent residents mean? | Penguins only | Scientists who study rock | *People who live there all the time | Tourists on a one-day trip
